Lightning CSS (build-time only, not shipped)
--------------------------------------------

`pnpm licenses list --prod` reports `lightningcss` (and its platform binary
`lightningcss-win32-x64-msvc`) under MPL-2.0. It is a **build tool**, not a bundled
dependency:

  - it is neither imported by any source file nor present in the shipped bundles —
    `packages/forgejo-toolkit/webview/vite.config.ts:44` only names it as Vite's CSS
    transformer, and it is declared in the extension's `devDependencies`;
  - `packages/forgejo-toolkit/.vscodeignore` excludes `node_modules/**`, so no
    lightningcss code or binary can end up in the `.vsix`;
  - it looks like a production dependency because `vue-router@5` declares `vite` as a
    peer dependency while pulling the Vite plugin machinery (`unplugin`) in as a real
    dependency, so `vite → lightningcss` is reachable from a production dependency.

No license obligation follows from running a build tool, and nothing of it is
distributed. Fixing the manifest graph itself (so `--prod` stops flagging it) would
mean dropping `css.transformer: 'lightningcss'` from `webview/vite.config.ts` and
using Vite's default esbuild CSS transformer instead; that is a build-config change
that needs a build to verify, so it is deliberately not made here.
